 "name": "rl-p2",
 "purpose": "P2: rl-p1 (design C's plan heads, docs/rl-es-plan.md section 21) with committed plans. rl-p1 re-drew every head every 50 rounds (~26 independent picks per game), so one pick governed ~4% of a game and its effect on the result was below the per-iteration noise (CORE's picks vs the result: t about 1 either way at iterations 7-8). Here a plan holds 500 rounds (DP.PLAN_EVERY; ~4.5 plans per game: first, epochs, the break, king-count changes) and the start explores more: plan_start --uniform 0.5 (half the mass uniform, p(zdb bin) 0.40-0.47, Fisher share 0.84-0.92; CORE's 12/8 at 0.073 against rl-p1's 0.010). Anchor zdpp7 (that start); zdb (zdpc00) tracked. Settings from rl-p1 iteration 2 (loose leash, lr 0.002); batch 256 because each head now has ~900 rows per iteration.",
